WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.720
I mean, this hurts to look at you

2
00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:03.990
I just have to tell you guys.

3
00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:07.890
You're so lovely and you're so beautifully dressed.

4
00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:11.410
And the fact that you're all from like tallest to smallest,

5
00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.330
I can't handle it.

6
00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:16.260
How did you guys get into the cookie business?

7
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:17.970 line:15%
First, we went to go ask her mom

8
00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.341 line:15%
would she approved of the business.

9
00:00:20.341 --> 00:00:23.510 line:15%
Then told us to go sit down with our dad.

10
00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:26.400
And our dad, eventually he agreed to do it.

11
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.630
And we came up with the name and the logo,

12
00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.630
and then it went off from there.

13
00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:34.010
Joshua, what has it been like working with your brothers

14
00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:35.780
and starting a business?

15
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.590
Well, it's been really fun to be able

16
00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:41.280
to work with my brothers, my mom and my dad.

17
00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.620 line:15%
And another thing that I really love is that

18
00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.690 line:15%
we're inspiring kids and adults across the world

19
00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:48.693 line:15%
to be entrepreneurs.

20
00:00:48.693 --> 00:00:50.260
(cheering and applause)

21
00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:51.670
That's so wise.

22
00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:54.300
Micah, you guys are going to school

23
00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.540
and running a successful business.

24
00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:58.933
How are you managing it all?

25
00:00:58.933 --> 00:01:02.220 line:15%
Well, how we're doing this is

26
00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:04.993 line:15%
we do our schoolwork first, then we bake the cookies.

27
00:01:06.824 --> 00:01:08.420
("awws" from audience)

28
00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:10.500
Caleb, what are you going to do

29
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.700
with the money you're making?

30
00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:15.270
Well, actually we created another business

31
00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:19.150 line:15%
called Kidpreneur Expo, which is an online platform

32
00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:23.360 line:15%
that allows kidpreneurs to advertise and market

33
00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:24.603 line:15%
in their business.

34
00:01:24.603 --> 00:01:26.380 line:15%
(cheering and applause)

35
00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:28.660
That's really smart.

36
00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:31.550
I learned early that marketing and advertising

37
00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:35.460
is very important because it's how you tell your story.

38
00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.672 line:15%
And it's a great way for you to take control

39
00:01:37.672 --> 00:01:42.000 line:15%
but also make sure it's exactly the way you see it.

40
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.020 line:15%
Isaiah, you are all such cool dudes.

41
00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:48.610
What would you tell someone who thought baking

42
00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:50.690
was a girl thing?

43
00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:53.810
Well, Drew, that's an awesome question.

44
00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:56.760
Let's say in my trip of imagination

45
00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.720
you're on a Saturday morning having some coffee

46
00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:03.660
probably just relaxing, and you have your cookies baking

47
00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:06.020
in the oven at 350 degrees.

48
00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:08.352
Then when they get out, you take a bite

49
00:02:08.352 --> 00:02:11.193
and ooey, gooey chocolate all over your mouth.

50
00:02:13.502 --> 00:02:15.270
And another thing, Drew,

51
00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:18.070
one of our biggest supporters was our grandfather.

52
00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:21.830
And he would always tell us whatever you put your mind to,

53
00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:23.430
you can always do it.

54
00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:27.410
I am so excited to be talking to you guys.

55
00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:31.910
And I know that you sent us some of your yummy cookies.

56
00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:34.200
Okay, yum, yum, yum, yum, yum, yum.

57
00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.320
What do we have?

58
00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:37.390
Walk me through it, gentlemen.

59
00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:40.350
All right, so we have the two face,

60
00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:43.360
which is double dark chocolate mixed with chocolate chip.

61
00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:48.360
Then we have chocolate chip, snicker doodle,

62
00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:52.780
then there's cookies and cream, Papa's white chocolate

63
00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:55.630
macadamia nut that was named after our grandfather

64
00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:59.120
because he loved macadamia nuts.

65
00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:01.200
And then oatmeal.

66
00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.170
Hmm, hmm, hmm-hmm.

67
00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:10.330 line:15%
The cookie that we picked up for you, Drew

68
00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:15.330 line:15%
is Drew's ET cookie, which means extra tasty!

69
00:03:15.873 --> 00:03:17.822
(cheering and applause)

70
00:03:17.822 --> 00:03:20.272
I love it!

71
00:03:20.272 --> 00:03:25.272
Oh gosh, you gentlemen are so handsome and so talented.

72
00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:27.697
Hm, oh my gosh.

73
00:03:27.697 --> 00:03:30.420
[Billinglea Brother] In the Drew cookies there's pecans,

74
00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:32.800
toffee and chocolate chip.

75
00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:37.800 line:15%
I must tell you guys, these are truly some

76
00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:40.410 line:15%
of the best cookies I've ever had in my life.

77
00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:41.970
And I'm not just saying that.

78
00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:43.500
These are perfect.

79
00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:46.820
Their texture is exactly what you dream of.

80
00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:48.760
And there are so many different flavors

81
00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:50.970
from all the different nuts.

82
00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:52.240
They're incredible.

83
00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:56.120
You guys have made an extraordinary product, and I know

84
00:03:56.120 --> 00:04:00.200
that one of your goals is to sell your cookies nationwide.

85
00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:05.200
And I actually heard that you would love to sell in a store.

86
00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:10.080
And I reached out to the owners of Slim and Husky's,

87
00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:14.710
the first Black-owned pizza franchise in the country.

88
00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:18.290
We love that place, we go there all the time.

89
00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:19.720
Their food is great.

90
00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:24.260
Their successful pizza empire has stores nationwide,

91
00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:28.240
and I would love to welcome in the wonderful co-owners

92
00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:32.468
of Slim and Husky's, Clint, EJ, and Derek.

93
00:04:32.468 --> 00:04:35.801 line:15%
(cheering and applause)

94
00:04:37.638 --> 00:04:38.640 line:15%
What's up fellas?

95
00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:40.240 line:15%
It is great to meet you guys.

96
00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:42.380 line:15%
We wanted to hop on and say congratulations

97
00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:43.970
on all you guys' success.

98
00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:46.360
You guys are true leaders for your communities

99
00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:47.350
and your families.

100
00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:49.340
I just want to tell you to keep on going.

101
00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:51.190
The best is yet to come for you guys.

102
00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:54.649
Man, we just want you guys to know if you focus,

103
00:04:54.649 --> 00:04:57.230
continue doing what you love

104
00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.990
with the people that you love, man

105
00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:03.250
you can't go wrong so much success to you guys.

106
00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:05.130
What we're going to do is allow you guys

107
00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:07.270
sell your cookies in out Atlanta stores.

108
00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:08.369
How does that sound?

109
00:05:08.369 --> 00:05:10.169
(cheering and applause)

110
00:05:10.169 --> 00:05:12.090
That's great, let's go!

111
00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:13.180
Awesome, awesome.

112
00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:14.440
So what we'll do is we'll work together

113
00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:15.920
on a marketing strategy and we'll figure out

114
00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:16.960
